{"availability":"available","full":"subhajitlucky/cscosmos","name":"cscosmos","description":"CSCosmos is mapping the universe of Computer Science into approachable, visual, and interactive microsites—covering everything from browser internals to distributed consensus.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-12-07T09:19:28Z","updated":"2026-10-17T09:07:22Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cscosmos.vercel.app","topics":["computer-science","education","learning","nextjs","react","typescript","visualization","vite"],"demo":"https://cscosmos.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:37.308Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:37.308Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:46:37.308Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:39:42.647Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-13T02:09:36.371Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T02:46:37.308Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CSCosmos is an interactive computer science visualizer hub and learning platform, organizing 245 curated topics across 8 core domains with natively absorbed interactive visualization engines.","Computer science topics are usually scattered across separate articles, demos, videos, and one-off visualizers. CSCosmos organizes them into one navigable map so learners can move from fundamentals to advanced systems without losing context.","The goal is not to publish a static list. The hub acts as an index for a growing set of focused microsites where each topic can eventually become an interactive visual learning module — natively absorbed into the platform."],"features":["Portfolio case study:","Status: Live platform"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/subhajitlucky/cscosmos/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"476244e932679051384e31fb4aad1a6d686908bea4df9e7315bdad9b21268dfa","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:42.931Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10